  "limitations": [
    "Protected skin means the fixed RGB heuristic family, not a semantic face mask or equality of every facial pixel.",
    "Alpha is exact everywhere. RGB is unchanged where alpha<240; near-opaque pixels with alpha 240 through 254 may change RGB.",
    "The temporal diagnostic uses unaligned screen pixels with source RGB difference<=2, equal alpha>=250 and four near-opaque cardinal neighbors. It is not motion-compensated and is not a complete flicker or perceptual quality score.",
    "Both candidates introduce additional RGB jumps on the evaluated source-stable pixels; threshold-sensitivity counts are retained without claiming a temporal improvement.",
    "GIFs use fixed 256-color matte palettes and centisecond timing; RGBA atlases and source schedules are authoritative."
